Every evidence unit:

```json
{
  "evidence_id": "ev_...",
  "atom_id": "c1",

  "source": {
    "url": "...",
    "title": "...",
    "domain": "...",
    "source_type": "PRIMARY|SECONDARY|STRUCTURED",
    "published_at": "...",
    "retrieved_at": "..."
  },

  "stance": "SUPPORT|REFUTE|NEUTRAL",

  "span": "...",

  "directness": 0.91,
  "authority": 0.84,
  "freshness": 0.99,

  "request_hash": "...",
  "content_hash": "..."
}
```

This is worth copying from GAVEL conceptually.

GAVEL's central mechanism is an **Evidence Contract** binding atomic subclaims to explicit evidence units, followed by deterministic scrutiny of identifiers and cited spans. Its ablations found both evidence binding and mechanized citation validation important. ([ACL Anthology][16])

So:

```text
NO evidence without:
claim atom
source
exact span
retrieval timestamp
stance
content hash
```

